  {
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=x^{2} - x + 3$ at the point $(0,3)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Differentiate the polynomial.\n\n$$\nf'(x)=2 x - 1.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_t=f'(0)&=2 (0) - 1=-1, \\\\m_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\\frac{1}{(-1)}=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $(0,3)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-(3)&=1(x-(0)), \\\\y&=x + 3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=1x+(3), \\\\x&=-3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $(-3,0)$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
